# GitHub CLI Integration

Use `gh` for all GitHub operations. Do not use the GitHub web UI when `gh` can do the job.

## Prerequisites

Before using `gh`, verify:

```powershell
gh --version
gh auth status
```

If not installed on Windows:

```powershell
winget install --id GitHub.cli -e --accept-source-agreements --accept-package-agreements
gh auth login
```

## Branch and PR Workflow

1. One Task ID per branch: `feature/<TaskID>-<short-name>`.
2. Push with upstream: `git push -u origin HEAD`.
3. Create PRs with `gh pr create`; use a HEREDOC for the body.
4. Return the PR URL after creation.

Example:

```powershell
git checkout -b feature/P-04-knowledge-ui
git push -u origin HEAD
gh pr create --title "feat(console): knowledge base upload page (P-04)" --body @"
## Summary
- Add knowledge base upload UI with drag-and-drop and file list states

## Test plan
- [ ] Upload PDF/DOCX/TXT/MD under 20MB
- [ ] Verify loading, empty, error, success states
- [ ] Check mobile layout
"@
```

## Common Commands

| Task | Command |
|---|---|
| View PR | `gh pr view --comments` |
| Check CI | `gh pr checks` |
| List issues | `gh issue list` |
| View issue | `gh issue view <number>` |
| Create repo | `gh repo create <name> --private --source=. --remote=origin --push` |

## Rules

- Never force-push to `main` or `master`.
- PR titles should include the Task ID when applicable.
- Link dependent PRs in the body, for example `Depends on #123`.
- Use `gh pr create` instead of opening PRs manually in the browser.
